From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reindert Pelsma <reindert.pelsma@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:12:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] hw/virtio: add virtio-nvgpu to virtio_device_names[]

virtio_id_to_name() asserts

    assert(device_id < G_N_ELEMENTS(virtio_device_names));

and virtio_device_names[] in QEMU 11.1 stops at VIRTIO_ID_SPI (45).
nvkvm's device is virtio device ID 50 (VIRTIO_ID_NVGPU in
src/qemu/virtio_nvgpu.h, which must stay in step with the same constant
in src/guest/nvkvm.h), so without this entry the array is too short and
QEMU aborts the first time anything asks the device for its name --
which happens during virtio realize, i.e. every boot.

The entry is written as a bare [50] rather than [VIRTIO_ID_NVGPU]
because that constant is nvkvm's, not upstream's: it is not in
include/standard-headers/linux/virtio_ids.h and the device is not
registered with the virtio spec.  Spelling the number out keeps this
patch to one file and makes it obvious that it is a downstream
squatting on an unassigned ID.  If the ID is ever assigned upstream,
this patch is what has to change.

The designated initialiser also sizes the array to 51, so IDs 42-49
become NULL entries.  That is not a new hazard: virtio_id_to_name()
asserts name != NULL immediately after the bounds check, so an
unassigned ID aborts either way -- it just now aborts on the second
assert instead of the first.  Nothing in QEMU 11.1 constructs those IDs.

9.2 -> 11.1 rebase note: upstream added [VIRTIO_ID_SPI] = "virtio-spi"
(ID 45) as the new last entry, so the trailing-comma hunk moved from the
GPIO line to the SPI line.  ID 50 is still unassigned in
include/standard-headers/linux/virtio_ids.h as of v11.1.1 (the highest
assigned is SPI at 45), so the squat is unchanged and still safe.
---
 hw/virtio/virtio.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio.c b/hw/virtio/virtio.c
index daa5607338..c2cf2732fd 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio.c
@@ -198,7 +198,8 @@ const char *virtio_device_names[] = {
     [VIRTIO_ID_AUDIO_POLICY] = "virtio-audio-pol",
     [VIRTIO_ID_BT] = "virtio-bluetooth",
     [VIRTIO_ID_GPIO] = "virtio-gpio",
-    [VIRTIO_ID_SPI] = "virtio-spi"
+    [VIRTIO_ID_SPI] = "virtio-spi",
+    [50] = "virtio-nvgpu",
 };
 
 static const char *virtio_id_to_name(uint16_t device_id)
